[node name="KingBooArena" type="Node3D" unique_id=2000134843]
metadata/_sms_note = "Pass 153: KING BOO'S ARENA -- the casino's great roulette table (the three discs at one height, the game's layout) with King Boo over its centre, and (153k) the casino boss room round it: the BossWall child, the game's own wall and ceiling (KingBooWall.tscn), a 33-m drum the outer disc's rim pokes into, so Mario cannot fall off. Drop it into the level where the table should be: the discs' walking faces are 1.1 to 1.9 m BELOW this node (the centre disc lowest), the outer ring 34 m across, the wall's paint runs from 13 m under the node to 47 m over it (its collision from 27 m under), the ceiling closes it at 47 m. King Boo finds the discs by himself (sms_roulette). The centre disc's pond (the game's water the player refills from) is solid floor here: add one of your sms_water Area3D volumes over it (7 m radius, the face at -1.9 m) if you want it to hold water. The room's knobs (CeilingOn, RoomCastsShadows, Brightness...) are on the BossWall child."

